    summary: 'A jiangshi is a reanimated corpse, stiff with rigor mortis, that attacks the living to draw their life-force (qi). Known from 18th-century collections of strange tales, it became the "hopping vampire" of 1980s Hong Kong cinema.',
    overview: 'Jiangshi are not spirits that tempt but bodies that will not rest — typically because of improper burial, a violent death, or a lingering po (the bodily soul). They are blind, sense breath, and move stiffly; later lore says they hop with arms outstretched. Defences include holding one\'s breath, mirrors, peach-wood, sticky rice, and Daoist paper talismans.',
