    overview: 'Medieval tales present tengu as kite-like beings that trick or possess Buddhist practitioners, especially proud monks; arrogant clergy were said to fall into the "tengu path" (tengudō). Later images show the red-faced, long-nosed daitengu dressed as a mountain ascetic (yamabushi), and the legend of Sōjōbō teaching swordsmanship to Minamoto no Yoshitsune on Mount Kurama.',
